From 0faa4587991ccdbe94cb862d64a55cf3d553f7b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:32:57 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 09/38] feat(replay): engine.dequeue on path B: a request still
 waiting in its rank's queue is handed back and placed again, off unless the
 policy keeps dispatched requests

KvAction::Dequeue { request_id } (engine.dequeue@1.0). When the placement policy asks for it
(PlacementPolicy::retains_dispatched), aggregated replay keeps a copy of each dispatched request
until its prefill completes. A dequeue of a request that is on that rank, not in the rank's
pending pass, not being tokenized and whose prefill has not completed cancels it on the rank
(CancelRequest, pending output discarded), reports Done and asks the policy to place it again
(PlacementPolicy::requeued); the placement is dispatched from the kept copy and the request's
record takes the new worker. Anything else is Failed. Tests: a waiting request moves to an idle
rank and starts at once; a request that already ran is not handed back.
